The legal text is the Constitution of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia, Proclamation No. 1/1995, Federal Negarit Gazeta no. 1, 21 August 1995, copied from the Equipo Nizkor / Derechos Human Rights site, https://www.derechos.org/intlaw/doc/eth2.html (retrieved 30 October 2026). The host is credited as the source of the bytes; it is not the publisher of the law and Lexifina makes no claim about its terms of use.

Official legal texts are not protected by copyright in Ethiopia. Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Protection Proclamation No. 410/2004 (Federal Negarit Gazeta no. 55, 19 July 2004), Article 5, 'Subject Matter not protected':

  "Notwithstanding the Provisions of Articles 2, 3 and 4 of this Proclamation the following matters shall not be protected; ... b) Any official text of a legislative, administrative or of legal nature, as well as official translations thereof."

The other proclamations are copied from the bilingual Federal Negarit Gazette issues (English column), using the issue PDFs hosted by MetaAppz (https://www.metaappz.com/), which is credited as the source of the bytes; it is not the publisher of the law.

Changes made by Lexifina: each text was converted to one Markdown file per article (from the HTML page for the Constitution, from the PDF text layer for the proclamations), one paragraph or item per line; line wraps, spacing and quotation marks were normalised; Chapter, Part and Section headings, the Amharic column, running heads and page numbers were left out. The wording of the law was not changed.

